FADE TO:

INT. CAFE - DAY

The Sound of Coffee machine steam in the background. JOHN and JANE sip their coffee. John sips his coffee while Jane take a bite of her cookie. They both look at Jane's laptop screen.

JOHN
What is this application?

JANE
This is a free Screenwriting app called  OpenDraft which uses "fountain" syntax

JOHN wonders. He looks confused.

JOHN
What is fountain?

JANE
Fountain is a markup language designed for writing screenplays. In this application you can write in fountain markup on the left pane and view it in the form of a screenplay on the right pane.

JOHN
Oh wow!

JANE
You can also hide or show the preview pane. You can print the script as well as export it as PDF by printing as PDF.

John wonders again. He takes another sip and puts down the cup.

JOHN
How can I find the syntax for fountain?

JANE
Just visit https://fountain.io/syntax/

JANE
(continues)
You can click on the top left to open left bar and create a New script by clicking "+ New Script" button. It will ask for a name. Just give it a name and start typing. You can make multiple scripts and all these are saved on your browser.

JOHN
What do you mean "saved on my browser"?

JANE
The data for your script is stored on the browser, if you ever delete or Browser data your scripts will be gone. But until then every time you open this browser with the same profile your scripts will be available. you can edit them and they will be saved automatically.

JOHN
So how about if I want to save them somewhere else?

JANE
You can click "Ctrl + S" to save the file as a .fountain or .md or .txt. You can also open a file by pressing "Ctrl + O".

JOHN
Impressive!

JANE
Remember, if you want to add notes, you use double curly brackets { like these not the double square brackets [.

{{This is a sample note.}}

JANE
(continues)
You can also show or hide notes for preview and print by pressing "Ctrl + m"

JOHN
Looks Great!

JANE
Wait! There is a lot more. You can definitely save and open your files or chose to keep the files in the browser itself, but you can also Export your entire collection to a JSON file and reload it as well. This could help you keep backups and restore in case you lose your browser data.

JOHN
This is awesome. Does it have auto-complete feature?

JANE
Of course! If you type the INT. or EXT. at the beginning of a line you will be shown a list of previously present scenes. If you type character names in all caps, any character that has had a dialog previously will show up and you can select the one you want.

JOHN
This is making me think that maybe I should start writing the screenplay for my next big film or series.

JANE
Of course, you should. And in case you are confused about what scenes would come first or last, you can rearrange the order of the scenes. Just click on the Board View, which will open a Cork Board View where you can see the scenes as post it slips. Let's change the setting go to a dream sequence.

FADE TO:

EXT. SURFACE OF THE MOON - DAY  

John and Jane are now in a dream sequence. Both are wearing a space suit

JANE
(old speaker voice)
So now that we have 2 scenes. You can move them around till you are happy with your sequence. You can also alter the scenes within the Cork Board View. If you are happy, you can save changes and close the Cork Board View. The changes made int he Board view will reflect in your script.

John is really surprised to be on the moon. He looks around.

JOHN
Wow! This is how Neil and Buzz felt like back in 1969.

JANE
(continues)
Let's not get lost here in the dream world let's go back to the cafe so that we can showcase the Cork Board View.

INT. CAFE - DAY

John and Jane are back at the table in the cafe. 

JANE
So now, what do you think of Open Draft?

JOHN
I think I am loving it. What is that?

John presses the "Outliner" button. It opens the Outline view on the right side.

JOHN
Oh! I can see all my scenes in the outline window on the right. What happens when I click on one.

JANE
It will take you to that scene.

JOHN
This is really starting to make me think that I have been writing screenplays the wrong way all my life. 

JANE
Well, let's not get carried away. I know these features are amazing but, OpenDraft is still a new, simple open source, web-based app, made by one person in his free time, so it definitely is NOT the best. but it is a great start, especially because it is FREE and open source. It will definitely get better with time as more users use it and give their feedback. If you would like to make it better, please go to GitHub and start making it better. 

{{http://https://github.com/ArcTropics/fountain-screenplay}}